css/base.css (helpers)<pre><code>.container {
  width: min(100% - 2 * var(--space-4), var(--container));
  margin-inline: auto;
}

.visually-hidden {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip-path: inset(50%);
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.skip-link:focus {
  top: var(--space-2);
  left: var(--space-2);
  z-index: 100;
  width: auto;
  height: auto;
  clip-path: none;
  padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  background: var(--surface);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
}

.btn {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background: var(--brand);
  color: #fff;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: none;
  cursor: pointer;
}
.btn:hover {
  background: var(--brand-dark);
}
.btn--outline {
  background: var(--surface);
  color: var(--brand);
  border-color: var(--brand);
}
.btn--outline:hover {
  background: var(--brand-soft);
}

:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid var(--accent);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
</code></pre> Code What it does <code>.container { width: min(100% - 2 * var(--space-4), var(--container)); }</code> The width is the smaller of "full width minus 16 px each side" and 1200 px. One line gives side padding on phones and a max width on desktops. <code>margin-inline: auto;</code> Equal left and right margins, which centres the box. <code>inline</code> means "left/right" in left-to-right languages. <code>.visually-hidden { … }</code> Hides text visually but keeps it for screen readers. Used for form labels the design doesn't show. (<code>display: none</code> would hide it from screen readers too.) <code>.skip-link:focus { … }</code> The "Skip to main content" link is hidden until a keyboard user presses Tab; then it appears in the corner. <code>.btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; … }</code> Turns the button into a small flex row, so an icon and text line up in the middle. <code>gap</code> is the space between them. <code>border: 1px solid transparent;</code> A transparent border, so the outline variant (which has a visible border) is exactly the same size. <code>cursor: pointer;</code> Shows the hand cursor. <code>.btn:hover</code> Darker green when the mouse is over it. <code>.btn--outline</code> The modifier: white background, green text and border. <code>:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--accent); }</code> A thick yellow ring when someone uses the keyboard. <code>:focus-visible</code> (unlike <code>:focus</code>) doesn't show it on mouse clicks. Never remove focus outlines without replacing them.

